      "id": 1,
      "text": "Riceville was platted in 1855 by the Rice brothers—Leonard, Dennis, and Gilbert—who gave the town its name.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Riceville%2C_Iowa"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s growth followed an old Indian trail that crossed the Wapsipinicon River and led toward the west, with a spring that now supplies the town’s water works.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://iagenweb.org/mitchell/localdat/ricevill.htm"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1901 a devastating fire destroyed much of Riceville, after which the community rebuilt and reshaped its downtown.",
